# fixedbugs, defect 2049, 2026-10-13, the defect's fourth reproducer.
#
# SYMPTOM: a header of the program's own writing `HeroSt` was told
# `internal error: compiling the generated C failed` at exit 2: clang's
# `unknown type name 'HeroSt'; did you mean 'HeroStr'?` at the header's
# line, its note at `heroes_runtime.h`'s `HeroStr`, and a note in the
# runtime's files was the compiler's.
#
# FIX: the note is told as the Heroes runtime's own name clang
# suggests, the header refused at its line 3, exit 1, with no fix: clang's
# own suggestion is the runtime's type (`cli/runtime_name.hero`).

extern "fixedbugs-2049-a-header-that-misspells-the-runtime-s-string-type-is-refused.h"  #~ ffi_header_refused
    function eight() -> i32

function main()
    print(eight())
